You are building a production-grade SaaS called Nexus.

## STACK

- Next.js 15 (App Router ONLY)
- TypeScript strict mode
- Tailwind CSS
- React Query for server state
- Zustand for client state

## ARCHITECTURE RULES

- Use modular architecture (/modules)
- Separate UI, business logic, and API layers strictly
- No business logic inside components
- No hardcoded data anywhere

## NEXT.JS RULES

- Always use Server Components by default
- Use "use client" only when required
- Never use pages/ directory
- Fetch data in Server Components using async/await
- Avoid useEffect for data fetching

## CODING RULES

- Always write reusable components
- Prefer composition over duplication
- Keep functions small and single-purpose
- Use TypeScript interfaces for all data models

## API RULES

- All API calls must go through /lib/api
- No direct fetch inside UI components

## UI RULES

- Card-based design system only
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Search-first UX (Airbnb style)

## BUSINESS LOGIC RULES

- Marketplace, CRM, Bookings, Events are separate modules
- Modules must NOT depend on each other directly
- Shared logic goes in /lib or /services

## QUALITY RULE

Before finalizing code:
- Ensure no duplication
- Ensure correct folder placement
- Ensure TypeScript safety
- Ensure clean separation of concerns
